ChromaLight
Copyright (c) 2026 N[i]ghtly. All rights reserved.

The source code is published so people can read it, learn from it, report bugs
and send fixes. It is not open source. The code and assets stay the property of
the author.

You may:

1. Download the mod from the official pages (GitHub, Modrinth, CurseForge) and
   use it for yourself, including on any server, in videos and streams.
2. Include the unmodified mod in a modpack, as long as the modpack downloads it
   from Modrinth or CurseForge, or links to one of the official pages.
3. Read and study the source code, build it for your own use, and send changes
   back to this repository as pull requests. By sending a pull request you agree
   that it can be included in ChromaLight under this license.
4. Write add-ons and light packs that use ChromaLight's public API
   (dev.nightmode.chromalight.api) or its light pack format.

You may not, without written permission from the author:

1. Copy any part of the code, shaders or assets into another mod, program or
   project, whether or not it is changed, and whether or not it is free.
2. Publish modified versions or forks of ChromaLight, or ports to other
   Minecraft versions or mod loaders.
3. Reupload the mod files to any other site or distribute them in any other way
   than described above.
4. Sell the mod or any part of it, or put it behind a paywall.

To ask for permission, open an issue at
https://github.com/notsoboreal/ChromaLight/issues

